[38;2;124;124;124m**The values N, N-1, N-2, ..., N-k must all fit in rows 0 through k.**[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mRows 0 through k have n + (n-1) + ... + (n-k) = (k+1)(2n-k)/2 slots.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThe number of values that must fit in rows 0 through k is the number of values v[0m[38;2;124;124;124mwith N-v ≤ k, i.e., v ≥ N-k. That's k+1 values: N, N-1, ..., N-k.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo we need k+1 ≤ (k+1)(2n-k)/2, i.e., 1 ≤ (2n-k)/2, i.e., k ≤ 2n-2. This is [0m
[38;2;124;124;124malways true for k ≤ n-1. So no contradiction from this simple counting.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mBut we can be more precise. The values N, N-1, ..., N-k must fit in rows 0 [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mthrough k, AND the remaining slots in rows 0 through k must be filled with [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mvalues ≤ N-k-1. The number of remaining slots is (k+1)(2n-k)/2 - (k+1) = (k+1)[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m(2n-k-2)/2.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThe number of values ≤ N-k-1 is N-k-1. These must fit in the remaining slots of [0m[38;2;124;124;124mrows 0 through k PLUS all slots in rows k+1 through n-1. The total number of [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mslots for values ≤ N-k-1 is (k+1)(2n-k-2)/2 + sum_{j=k+1}^{n-1} (n-j) = (k+1)[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m(2n-k-2)/2 + (n-k-1)(n-k)/2.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mAnd N-k-1 = n(n+1)/2 - k - 1. We need N-k-1 ≤ (k+1)(2n-k-2)/2 + (n-k-1)(n-k)/2.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet me compute the right side:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m(k+1)(2n-k-2)/2 + (n-k-1)(n-k)/2[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m= [(k+1)(2n-k-2) + (n-k-1)(n-k)] / 2[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m= [2n(k+1) - (k+1)(k+2) + (n-k-1)(n-k)] / 2[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m= [2n(k+1) - (k+1)(k+2) + n^2 - n(2k+1) + k(k+1)] / 2[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m= [2nk + 2n - k^2 - 3k - 2 + n^2 - 2nk - n + k^2 + k] / 2[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m= [n + n^2 - 2k - 2] / 2[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m= [n^2 + n - 2k - 2] / 2[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m= [n(n+1) - 2(k+1)] / 2[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m= N - (k+1)[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo the number of available slots for values ≤ N-k-1 is N - (k+1). And the number[0m[38;2;124;124;124mof such values is N-k-1. So we need N-k-1 ≤ N-(k+1) = N-k-1. Equality! So the [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mconstraint is tight: every slot must be filled with the correct value.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThis means the counting argument is tight and doesn't give a contradiction. The [0m[38;2;124;124;124mvalues can potentially be placed correctly.[0m

